index 0000000000..75ce8c0a9b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.cursor/rules/generated-sdks-and-types.mdc
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+---
+description: Do not hand-edit OpenAPI-generated SDK code or scripted assisted-service types; use Yarn workspace generate/update scripts instead.
+globs:
+  - libs/sdks/**
+  - libs/types/**
+alwaysApply: false
+---
+
+# Generated SDK and API types
+
+## Do not edit by hand
+
+- **`libs/sdks/lib/**`** — OpenAPI Generator output (e.g. `apis/`, `models/`, `common.ts`). Files include headers such as “Do not edit the class manually.”
+- **`libs/types/assisted-installer-service.d.ts`** — Produced by `libs/types/scripts/update-assisted-installer-service-types.js`.
+
+## Use these commands (from repo root)
+
+**SDKs (`@openshift-assisted/sdks`):**
+
+```bash
+yarn workspace @openshift-assisted/sdks run generate-sdk:all
+```
+
+Or one service:
+
+```bash
+yarn workspace @openshift-assisted/sdks run generate-sdk:production:assisted-installer-service
+yarn workspace @openshift-assisted/sdks run generate-sdk:production:accounts-management-service
+yarn workspace @openshift-assisted/sdks run generate-sdk:production:authorization-service
+```
+
+**Types — assisted installer service only (`@openshift-assisted/types`):**
+
+```bash
+yarn workspace @openshift-assisted/types run update:assisted-installer-service
+```
+
+Optional version tag argument is supported by that script (see its usage in `libs/types/scripts/update-assisted-installer-service-types.js`).
+
+## Allowed edits (not regenerated output)
+
+- **`libs/sdks`:** Generator inputs and config, e.g. `openapitools.json`, `.openapi-generator-ignore`, and similar — not files under `lib/` that are generator output.
+
+## Other `libs/types` `.d.ts` files
+
+`accounts-management-service.d.ts` and `authorization-service.d.ts` are not updated by `update:assisted-installer-service`. If they need changes and no script exists, align with team process or add a generation script — do not assume they are safe to patch like the assisted-service output.
diff --git a/.cursor/rules/translations.mdc b/.cursor/rules/translations.mdc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..63b1af81ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.cursor/rules/translations.mdc
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+---
+description:
+  Translation strings in libs/ui-lib (source) and libs/locales catalogs; use yarn
+  process_new_strings for English; do not hand-edit translation JSON or non-English locale files.
+globs:
+  - libs/locales/**
+  - libs/ui-lib/**
+alwaysApply: false
+---
+
+# Translation strings
+
+Source strings live in **`libs/ui-lib`** (`t('ai:…')`). The English catalog
+**`libs/locales/lib/en/translation.json`** is produced by `yarn process_new_strings`; other locale
+files are out of scope for agents.
+
+## Workflow
+
+1. Add or change strings in TS/TSX using `t("ai:string for translation")` (or `t('ai:…')` — match
+   project style).
+2. From repo root:
+
+```bash
+yarn process_new_strings
+```
+
+Root `package.json` maps this to the `@openshift-assisted/locales` workspace script.
+
+**Whenever translation strings change in source** (new keys, reworded copy, or removed `t('ai:…')`
+usage), run `yarn process_new_strings` so `libs/locales/lib/en/translation.json` stays in sync.
+
+3. **Optional — validation:**
+
+```bash
+yarn workspace @openshift-assisted/locales run validate_translation_files
+```
+
+## What to avoid
+
+- **`libs/locales/lib/en/translation.json`** — Only updated by `process_new_strings` /
+  i18next-parser. Do not add or change keys here by hand; use the workflow above.
+- **`lib/es/`, `lib/fr/`, `lib/ja/`, `lib/ko/`, `lib/zh/`** — Handled by a separate localization
+  process. **Do not edit** those `translation.json` files.
+
+## Allowed edits
+
+Config and tooling under `libs/locales` that are not translation catalogs (e.g.
+`.i18next-parser.config.cjs`, scripts) when intentionally changing the pipeline — not routine string
+changes.
